==Trivia==
*He is more than likely a reference to the ''[[wikipedia:Dragon Quest|Dragon Quest]]'' character [[wikia:dragonquest:Hargon|Hargon]], as besides having similar designs, both are evil priests who aim to summon skull-wearing demonic gods of destruction ([[wikia:dragonquest:Malroth|Malroth]] in Hargon's case, [[Lord of Ruin Jagando]] in High Priest Mamon's).
**Mamon's design also bears similarities to [[wikia:dragonquest:Killvearn|Killvearn]], another antagonist from the ''Dragon Quest'' franchise.
*Mamon and his little sister [[Grand Mage Mimon|Mimon]] have similar names to [[wikipedia:ja:マモー・ミモー|Mamō and Mimō]], a pair of [https://youtu.be/3_b43drGB18 comedy characters] from the variety show ''[[wikipedia:ja:ウッチャンナンチャンのやるならやらねば!|Ucchan Nanchan no Yarunara Yaraneba!]]''. Furthermore, Mimon and Mimō are both redheads.
*Mamon's name may also be derived from 魔 ''ma'' (demon), ''sermon'' (since he's a priest) and ''[[wikipedia:Mammon|Mammon]]'', a term from the [[wikipedia:New Testament|New Testament]] which has often been used as a name for a patron demon of greed. While Mamon isn't stated to desire money, the sin of greed includes overambition, and Mamon is highly ambitious indeed, plotting to rule the entirety of [[The Aku Realms]].
*Mamon sounds dangerously close to the Spanish insult ''Mamón'', so he's renamed as Babón in Spanish.
*He is The Aku Realms' narrator.
*His scepter bares a resemblance to [[Hevijak the Wicked (Uber Rare Cat)|Hevijak the Wicked]].
*The blue eyeball in his hand may be the "crystal of awakening" mentioned in [[The Aku Realms/OPED|The Aku Realms intro]].
*In the [[The Aku Realms/OPEDJP|Japanese Aku Realms opening/ending]], Mamon refers to himself using the archaic pronoun 我 ''ware'', which used to be the most popular Japanese first-person pronoun up until the [[wikipedia:Edo period|Edo period]], when it started to be phased out by 私 ''watashi''. Nowadays, it's considered too old-fashioned and formal to see much use outside of literary contexts. In fiction, it's mainly used by older, important, often immortal characters such as gods and demon lords.
*When Mamon is knocked back, his left hand sprite erroneously gains an extra finger.
*He is tied with Lord of Ruin Jagando for the highest [[Shield]] health of all [[:Category:Aku Enemies|Aku]].

